  "note": "Base text Luke 23:39-43. Every quoted verse was pasted verbatim from the Open Luganda Contemporary Bible (lug_bib), which matches the shipped Luganda corpus; the references above are the parts actually quoted (a/b marks a half-verse). FLAGGED FOR REVIEW — a genuine text-tradition divergence at Luke 23:42: Moody argues on the KJV word 'Lord' ('now he calls Him Lord'), but the OLCB reads the NAME «Yesu», not «Mukama». Per the no-put-words-in-the-Bible's-mouth rule the OLCB verse was pasted verbatim (Yesu) while Moody's surrounding commentary was translated faithfully (yamuyita «Mukama»); the editorial section heading he wrote is rendered «MUKAMA, ONZIJUKIRA». A native reviewer should decide whether to footnote this. Also noted: the English's 'eight thousand converted in two days' appears to conflate Acts 2:41/4:4 — rendered as-given, no verse pasted (none is quoted there)."
